# Deriving ADAE from AE + ADSL (CDISC ADaM)

Below is a complete, production-style SAS derivation. The core idea: start from SDTM **AE**, bring in the subject-level treatment window from **ADSL**, convert ISO‑8601 partial dates to numeric analysis dates, then derive the flags and duration.

---

## 1. Merge AE with ADSL

```sas
proc sort data=ae;   by usubjid; run;
proc sort data=adsl; by usubjid; run;

data adae0;
    merge ae     (in=inae)
         adsl   (in=inadsl
                 keep=usubjid studyid trt01a trt01an trtsdt trtedt
                       age ageu sex sex race ethnic saffl
                       /* + any population flags you need: */);
    by usubjid;
    if inae;                       /* keep AE records only */

    ** Carry forward ADSL treatment vars onto every AE row **;
    trt01a  = trt01a;
    trt01an = trt01an;
    saffl   = saffl;
run;
```

---

## 2. ASTDT / AENDT (numeric analysis dates + partial-date imputation)

AESTDTC / AEENDTC are ISO‑8601 character and may be partial (`YYYY`, `YYYY-MM`, `YYYY-MM-DD`). Impute conservatively:

* **Start (ASTDT)** → earliest plausible date (missing month → Jan, missing day → 01).
* **End (AENDT)** → latest plausible date (missing month → Dec, missing day → last day of month).

```sas
data adae1;
    set adae0;
    length astfull aenfull $10;

    /* ---- START DATE: impute to FIRST of period ---- */
    select;
        when (length(aestdtc) >= 10)              astfull = substr(aestdtc,1,10);
        when (length(aestdtc) = 7)                astfull = cats(aestdtc,'-01');   /* YYYY-MM -> -01 */
        when (length(aestdtc) = 4)                astfull = cats(aestdtc,'-01-01');/* YYYY -> -01-01 */
        otherwise                                 astfull = '';
    end;
    astdt = input(astfull, yymmdd10.);

    /* ---- END DATE: impute to LAST of period ---- */
    select;
        when (length(aeendtc) >= 10)              aenfull = substr(aeendtc,1,10);
        when (length(aeendtc) = 7)                aenfull = cats(aeendtc,'-',
                                       put(day(intnx('month',input(cats(aeendtc,'-01'),yymmdd10.),0,'e')),z2.));
        when (length(aeendtc) = 4)                aenfull = cats(aeendtc,'-12-31');
        otherwise                                 aenfull = '';
    end;
    aendt = input(aenfull, yymmdd10.);

    astdtc = astfull;   /* analysis date-time, char form */
    aendtc = aenfull;
run;
```

---

## 3. TRTEMFL — Treatment-Emergent Flag

Treatment-emergent = AE **starts on or after first dose**. Compare the **numeric** ASTDT to TRTSDT (handles partial dates correctly once imputed):

```sas
data adae2;
    set adae1;
    length trtemfl $1;
    if not missing(astdt) and not missing(trtsdt) then do;
        if astdt >= trtsdt then trtemfl = 'Y';
        else                     trtemfl = '';
    end;
    /* If start date unknown -> undetermined: set to '' and flag per sponsor rule */
run;
```

> Variant you'll see often: also require the AE ends no earlier than first dose, and treat pre‑treatment AEs (`astdt < trtsdt`) as `trtemfl=''`. For partial/unknown start dates some sponsors impute to the **latest** plausible date before deciding TE; pick one rule and document it.

---

## 4. AOCCFL & AOCCPFL — First-Occurrence Flags (treatment-emergent only)

* **AOCCFL** — first TEAE overall **per subject** (earliest start date).
* **AOCCPFL** — first TEAE **per preferred term (AEDECOD)** per subject.

Compute each with the sort order that defines "first", then merge the flags back.

```sas
/* 4a. AOCCFL: earliest TEAE per subject ----------------------------- */
proc sort data=adae2;
    by usubjid astdt aeseq;          /* earliest start first */
run;
data fl_subj(keep=usubjid aeseq aoccfl);
    set adae2;
    by usubjid;
    where trtemfl='Y';
    if first.usubjid then aoccfl='Y';
run;

/* 4b. AOCCPFL: earliest TEAE per subject x preferred term ----------- */
proc sort data=adae2;
    by usubjid aedecod astdt aeseq;
run;
data fl_pt(keep=usubjid aeseq aoccptfl);
    set adae2;
    by usubjid aedecod;
    where trtemfl='Y';
    if first.aedecod then aoccptfl='Y';
run;

/* 4c. Merge flags back onto the master set -------------------------- */
proc sql;
    create table adae3 as
    select a.*,
           coalesce(b.aoccfl,'')   as aoccfl,
           coalesce(c.aoccptfl,'') as aoccptfl
    from   adae2 as a
    left join fl_subj as b on a.usubjid=a.usubjid and a.aeseq=b.aeseq
    left join fl_pt   as c on a.usubjid=a.usubjid and a.aeseq=c.aeseq;
run;
```

> Match on **USUBJID + AESEQ** (the SDTM record key) so each flag lands on exactly the right AE row. (Many sponsors name the per-term flag `AOCCPFL`; I used `AOCCPFL` for the preferred-term flag per your list.)

---

## 5. ADURN — Analysis Duration (numeric, days)

```sas
data adae;
    set adae3;
    length aduru $8;
    if not missing(aendt) and not missing(astdt) then do;
        adur  = aendt - astdt;          /* exclusive */
        adurn = aendt - astdt + 1;      /* inclusive day count (standard for ADaM) */
        aduru = 'DAYS';
    end;
    format astdt aendt date9.;
run;
```

---

## Derivation Reference (quick table)

| Variable | Rule |
|---|---|
| **ASTDT** | numeric of AESTDTC; partial → impute to earliest (Jan 1 / day 01) |
| **AENDT** | numeric of AEENDTC; partial → impute to latest (Dec 31 / last day of month) |
| **TRTEMFL** | `='Y'` when `ASTDT >= TRTSDT` (numeric compare), else `''` |
| **AOCCFL** | `='Y'` on the earliest TEAE (by ASTDT) per subject |
| **AOCCPFL** | `='Y'` on the earliest TEAE (by ASTDT) per subject × preferred term (AEDECOD) |
| **ADURN** | `AENDT − ASTDT + 1` (days), `ADURU='DAYS'` |

---

## Key edge cases to lock down (document in reviewer's guide)

1. **Partial / missing AESTDTC** — imputation direction drives TE classification; state your rule explicitly.
2. **TRTSDT missing** (never dosed) — TEAE is undefined; usually `TRTEMFL=''` and the subject is excluded from the safety population (`SAFFL='Y'` analyses).
3. **AESEQ tie-break** — always sort with a secondary key so "first" is deterministic.
4. **Flags scope to TEAEs only** — `WHERE TRTEMFL='Y'` before assigning AOCCFL/AOCCPFL.
5. **Same-day AEs** — duration `ADURN` = 1 (not 0) because of the `+1` inclusive convention.

```
