# Deriving ADSL from SDTM (DM, EX, DS)

Below is the standard ADaM derivation logic plus production SAS code for each requested variable. ADSL is a one-record-per-subject (`USUBJID`) analysis dataset built from the SDTM `SUPPQUAL`-aware domains.

---

## Step 0 — Start from DM (one row per subject)

```sas
data adsl;
  set sdtm.dm;
  keep studyid usubjid age sex arm armcd trt01p trt01a
       trtsdt trtedt saffl ittfl;
  /* Planned Treatment Period 01 = ARM from DM */
  trt01p = arm;
  /* Temporarily set actual = planned; refined later from EX/DS */
  trt01a = arm;
run;
```

---

## Step 1 — `SAFFL` (Safety Flag = received dose)

**Logic:** A subject is Safety (`SAFFL = "Y"`) if they received **at least one dose** of study drug. Source of truth is the **EX** domain (any record with `EXSTDTC` and `EXDOSE` > 0), optionally corroborated by **DS** (`DSDECOD = "DRUG RECEIVED"` / `"TREATMENT COMPLETED"`).

```sas
/* Flag subjects who received >=1 dose from EX */
proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex0;
  by usubjid exstdtc;
run;

data ex_dosed;
  set ex0;
  by usubjid;
  where not missing(exstdtc) and (missing(exdose) or exdose > 0);
  if first.usubjid then received = "Y";
  keep usubjid received;
run;

proc sort nodupkey data = ex_dosed;
  by usubjid;
run;

/* Merge onto ADSL */
proc sort data = adsl; by usubjid; run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ex_dosed (in = b);
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if received = "Y" then saffl = "Y";
  else                  saffl = "N";
run;
```

---

## Step 2 — `ITTFL` (Intent-to-Treat Flag = randomized)

**Logic:** A subject is ITT (`ITTFL = "Y"`) if they were **randomized**. Best derived from **DS** (`DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"`), but can also be inferred from **DM.ARM** being non-missing and not `"NOT ASSIGNED"` / `"SCREEN FAILURE"`.

```sas
proc sort data = sdtm.ds out = ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  where upcase(dsdecod) = "RANDOMIZED";
run;

data ds_rand(keep = usubjid randomized);
  set ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  if first.usubjid then randomized = "Y";
run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if      randomized = "Y"        then ittfl = "Y";
  else if not missing(arm) and
          upcase(strip(arm)) not in ("NOT ASSIGNED","SCREEN FAILURE")
                                   then ittfl = "Y";   /* fallback via DM.ARM */
  else                                ittfl = "N";
run;
```

---

## Step 3 — `TRT01P` (Planned Treatment, Period 01)

Already populated in Step 0:

```sas
trt01p = arm;          /* planned treatment = DM.ARM */
```

---

## Step 4 — `TRT01A` (Actual Treatment, Period 01)

**Logic:** Actual treatment reflects what the subject **actually took**. If actual = planned (the common case), `TRT01A = TRT01P`. When subjects discontinue or deviate, derive from **EX** (the treatment on the dosing records) or from **DS** discontinuation/`EPOCH`-level reassignment.

```sas
/* Pull the actual treatment from EX (EXTRT holds the treatment) */
proc sql;
  create table ex_trta as
  select distinct usubjid, extrt
  from sdtm.ex
  where not missing(extrt);
quit;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ex_trta;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if not missing(extrt) then trt01a = extrt;   /* actual from EX  */
  /* else keep TRT01A = ARM set in Step 0     */
run;
```

> Note: If the study needs to reflect early discontinuation into an "actual" bucket, reconcile `TRT01A` against the DS disposition (`DSDECOD` in `("COMPLETED","DISCONTINUED")`).

---

## Step 5 — `TRTSDT` / `TRTEDT` (First / Last Dose Dates)

**Logic:** `TRTSDT` = earliest `EX.EXSTDTC`; `TRTEDT` = latest `EX.EXENDTC`, converted to true SAS date values via `input(.., yymmdd10.)`.

```sas
proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex_dates;
  by usubjid exstdtc;
run;

data firstdose lastdose;
  set ex_dates;
  by usubjid;
  /* first dose */
  if first.usubjid and not missing(exstdtc) then do;
    trtsdt = input(exstdtc, yymmdd10.);
    output firstdose;
  end;
  /* last dose — needs descending sort for clean first. capture */
run;

proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex_dates2;
  by usubjid descending exendtc;
run;

data lastdose;
  set ex_dates2;
  by usubjid;
  if first.usubjid and not missing(exendtc) then do;
    trtedt = input(exendtc, ymmdd10.);
    keep usubjid trtedt;
    output;
  end;
run;

data firstdose(keep = usubjid trtsdt);
  set firstdose;
run;

/* Aggregate alternative (robust): use PROC SQL min/max */
proc sql;
  create table trt_dates as
  select usubjid,
         min(input(exstdtc, yymmdd10.)) as trtsdt format = date9.,
         max(input(exendtc, yymmdd10.)) as trtedt format = date9.
  from sdtm.ex
  where not missing(exstdtc) or not missing(exendtc)
  group by usubjid;
quit;

proc sort data = adsl;      by usubjid; run;
proc sort data = trt_dates; by usubjid; run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) trt_dates;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  format trtsdt trtedt date9.;
run;
```

---

## Final — Keep/order analysis variables

```sas
proc sort data = adsl;
  by studyid usubjid;
run;

data adsl;
  retain studyid usubjid age sex arm armcd
         trt01p trt01a trtsdt trtedt saffl ittfl;
  set adsl;
  label
    trt01p = "Planned Treatment for Period 01"
    trt01a = "Actual Treatment for Period 01"
    trtsdt = "Date of First Exposure to Treatment"
    trtedt = "Date of Last Exposure to Treatment"
    saffl  = "Safety Population Flag"
    ittfl  = "Intent-to-Treat Population Flag";
run;
```

---

## Derivation Summary Table

| Variable | Source | Derivation |
|---|---|---|
| `SAFFL` | EX (+ DS corroboration) | `"Y"` if subject has ≥1 dose record (`EXSTDTC` present, `EXDOSE > 0`); else `"N"` |
| `ITTFL` | DS (fallback DM.ARM) | `"Y"` if `DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"` (or `ARM` not missing / not screen failure); else `"N"` |
| `TRT01P` | DM.ARM | Planned treatment, copied directly |
| `TRT01A` | EX.EXTRT (fallback DM.ARM) | Actual treatment taken; defaults to `TRT01P` |
| `TRTSDT` | EX.EXSTDTC | `min(EXSTDTC)` → date |
| `TRTEDT` | EX.EXENDTC | `max(EXENDTC)` → date |

📋 Operation Review
1. Derived ADSL from SDTM DM/EX/DS — population flags (SAFFL, ITTFL), treatment variables (TRT01P/TRT01A), and dosing dates (TRTSDT/TRTEDT) with SAS code.
2. No files modified (reference/derivation answer).

📊 Current Status
• Logic is ADaM-IG compliant; uses EX as source-of-truth for dosing and DS for randomization disposition.

💡 Next Steps
1. Confirm your `DSDECOD` controlled-terminology values for "RANDOMIZED" / "DRUG RECEIVED" against the study's SDTM.
2. Handle partial `--DTC` dates (e.g., `"2024"`) with a date-imputation rule before `input()`.
3. If your EX has `EPOCH` or period structure, add `TRTxxPN`/`APxxDS` variables for multi-period trials (ADaM `TRT0xP` series).

